[h1]Carrier: Autopilot Waypoints[/h1]
Give your carrier a route, choose engine power and return to commanding aircraft. Navigation and optional defensive automation use the [b]same aviation-control map[/b] as aircraft orders.

[h2]Plot a route without changing stations[/h2]
Drag your carrier icon to a destination, open [b]NAV[/b] in the upper-right corner and press [b]START AUTOPILOT[/b]. The carrier follows the game's native sea route while you work with your aircraft.

Use [b]+ POINT[/b], then click the map once, to extend the route, up to 20 points. Drag points to reposition them without deleting the following route. A short carrier click keeps the normal interaction. Aircraft orders, cameras and loadout windows continue through the original screen.

[b]To repeat a route, drop a waypoint onto another waypoint on the same carrier route.[/b] Drop the final point onto the first to loop the entire route. The points stay in place; the native repeat link closes the route and is visible with Revolution too.

Dragging the carrier itself replaces its previous route. [b]PAUSE AUTOPILOT[/b] releases automatic control and neutralizes propulsion; [b]CLEAR[/b] also removes the route. Ship inertia still applies. You can take over with the physical helm or throttle, then resume explicitly with Start.

[h2]Full native power, not an invented speed limit[/h2]
Choose [b]-10%[/b], [b]+10%[/b] or [b]FULL[/b] in the same panel. The range is 10-100%, default 100%. Actual speed is shown separately in knots.

[b]FULL allows the game's full native forward output.[/b] There is no fixed 25-knot or real-world maximum. Hull physics, engine condition, waves, turns and Revolution determine actual speed. Percentages are power settings, not guaranteed speeds; the mod does not force velocity or change hull thrust/drag.

[h2]Live helm controls and smoother turns[/h2]
The physical wheel and throttle lever follow live navigation commands. Forward power adjusts smoothly through turns instead of dropping into turn-in-place idle, then recovers towards your setting as the ship straightens. Native endpoint slowdown, engine output and fuel limits apply.

[h2]Defensive arming when a threat is detected[/h2]
Enable [b]DEFENCE: ON[/b] to arm relevant defensive systems when your team currently detects a threat by [b]radar OR visual contact[/b]. Depending on the threat, this can enable AA, CIWS and the game's native torpedo/countermeasure automation. Hidden enemies and friendly projectiles do not trigger it.

The game handles engagement and consumables. Offensive artillery, cruise missiles and offensive torpedo arming stay under normal control. There are no repeated countermeasure fire commands. Manual off switches are respected until you enable automation again. Disabling automation does not disarm systems already enabled.

Defence works independently of the route panel and can remain enabled while navigation is paused. It starts disabled in each new session.

[h2]Native saves and Revolution support[/h2]
Routes and navigation mode use native save data; an active saved route is adopted after loading. Power is a preference. Routes are not shared globally across saves.

Enable [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3460002110]original Revolution[/url] alongside this addon when using it. Its command permissions remain in force. The carrier route stays visible even when Revolution hides normal carrier waypoints. No Revolution files or full game screens are bundled. Island Airfields is optional.

[h2]Required DLL: CC2X SDK 0.10.0-dev[/h2]
[b]This mod requires the matching native dinput8.dll. Subscribing to the Workshop mod alone is not enough.[/b] The DLL supplies the carrier motion and control APIs that the game's ordinary Lua interface does not expose. It belongs to the separate [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833014670]CC2X SDK[/url]; no DLL is hidden inside this addon. SDK 0.9/0.8 cannot run its navigation.

Use Windows Carrier Command 2 1.5.18-r2. Choose one installation method below.

[h2]Recommended: install with CC2 ModLoader[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to Carrier: Autopilot Waypoints and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833014670]CC2X SDK[/url]. Wait for both downloads.
[*]Close the game. Download the ready Windows GUI from [url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/CC2-ModLoader/releases]CC2 ModLoader releases[/url]. Use a release that explicitly supports [b]SDK 0.10.0-dev[/b]; older builds do not recognize this runtime.
[*]Place [b]CC2ModLoader.exe[/b] beside [b]carrier_command.exe[/b] and open it. Select the verified game if asked.
[*]Select the SDK library and Carrier: Autopilot Waypoints, together with the other mods you want. Include original Revolution when using it. ModLoader prepares the combined mod and installs the reviewed SDK DLL through its reversible apply process.
[*]Wait for the selection to finish applying, then click [b]Launch[/b]. No terminal, compiler or technical configuration editing is needed.
[/olist]

ModLoader checks the game and exact DLL, backs up a recognized previous runtime and preserves unknown loaders. Resolve any reported incompatible-loader conflict before launching this addon.

[h2]Alternative: install the DLL manually[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to this mod and CC2X SDK and wait for the downloads. Close the game.
[*]Get [b]dinput8.dll[/b] from the [url=https://github.com/Dioramawhois/Carrier-Command-2-extender/releases/tag/0.10.0-dev]matching SDK 0.10.0-dev release[/url]. Use the DLL asset, or extract it from the Windows runtime ZIP. The full source ZIP is for developers.
[*]In Steam, right-click Carrier Command 2, choose [b]Manage > Browse local files[/b]. This opens the folder containing [b]carrier_command.exe[/b].
[*]If that folder already contains dinput8.dll, identify it and back up the existing CC2X loader before replacing it. Preserve an unrelated loader; this mod cannot use two different DLLs under the same filename.
[*]Copy the matching [b]dinput8.dll directly beside carrier_command.exe[/b]. Putting it only in a mods folder or leaving it inside an archive does not install the runtime.
[*]Enable Carrier: Autopilot Waypoints in the game's mod list, plus original Revolution if used, and restart the game.
[/olist]

For either method: open the aviation-control map, drag your carrier to a destination, then choose [b]NAV > START AUTOPILOT[/b].

[h2]Important: reinstall the DLL after SDK updates[/h2]
[b]Steam updating the Workshop SDK does not replace a manually copied game-folder DLL.[/b] After an SDK runtime update, close the game and copy the new matching DLL again. A Lua-addon update alone does not always require a new DLL; check its SDK requirement.

[b]We recommend CC2 ModLoader for installation and DLL updates.[/b] Use a release supporting the new SDK, finish Steam downloads, then let ModLoader apply the selected set before launching. It upgrades reviewed runtimes with a backup; future DLLs still need review. Close the game before replacing its DLL.


[h2]Client beta scope[/h2]
Windows CC2 1.5.18-r2, [b]local single-player only[/b]. The owner accepted the revised aviation-map navigation with Revolution; the functional files and exact tested SDK are preserved for this release. Live combat, countermeasure expenditure and broader save/load coverage have not been separately accepted. Remote multiplayer, dedicated servers and native macOS runtime are unsupported. Native sea routing is not a guarantee of collision avoidance.

